All exceptions capture a full stack trace on construction (standard .NET behaviour). `AuditFailureException` is documented as being raised on every failed audit write. Depending on throw frequency, this could be visible in profiling. Consider documenting that callers should not construct these exceptions in tight loops or swallowed `catch` blocks. Not a code change — a comment in `AuditFailureException`.

