```
In a Docker container, the working directory is the assembly location. This is typically acceptable, but the value is not configurable from `appsettings`. If the container uses a read-only filesystem layer (common in hardened production images), the relative write will fail silently or throw at startup. The path should be configurable or validated on startup.

