## 6. Performance

### 6.1 Reflection on every log call (`SensitiveFieldDestructuringPolicy.cs`, lines 72–84)

```csharp
var properties = value.GetType().GetProperties();
if (!ContainsSensitiveProperty(properties))
{ ... }
```
`Type.GetProperties()` is called for **every structured object in every log event**. This includes EF Core entities, DTOs, exceptions, and framework objects. In high-throughput scenarios (e.g. a request handler logging 20+ structured values), this translates to hundreds of reflective calls per second.

**Fix**: Cache the `PropertyInfo[]` results per `Type` in a `ConcurrentDictionary<Type, PropertyInfo[]>` at the class level. Also cache the `bool HasSensitiveProperty` result per `Type` so `ContainsSensitiveProperty` is only called once per type lifetime:

```csharp
private static readonly ConcurrentDictionary<Type, (PropertyInfo[] Props, bool HasSensitive)>
    _typeCache = new();
```

### 6.2 `flushToDiskInterval: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2)` is appropriate but undocumented for Production

**`SerilogConfiguration.cs`, line 141**

A 2-second flush interval is a reasonable trade-off between durability and I/O. However, in the event of a hard crash, up to 2 seconds of log events could be lost. The comment should state this explicitly so operators understand the risk. In high-compliance deployments consider `flushToDiskInterval: null` (flush on every write) or bumping `shared: true` + `flushToDiskInterval: TimeSpan.Zero`, at the cost of throughput.

### 6.3 `WriteTo.Conditional` — no missing NuGet package guard at runtime

As noted in §3.2, `Serilog.Sinks.Conditional` is not in the `.csproj`. The build will fail before this performance concern materialises, but it is worth noting that even if the package were present, `WriteTo.Conditional` evaluates its predicate per log event. Since `isProduction` is captured as a `bool` in the closure and never changes, this is not a hot-path concern — but using `if (isProduction) ... else ...` on two separate `.WriteTo.Console(...)` calls would be marginally more efficient and removes the external package dependency.

